{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>On account of the cluster which the children of Israel cut from there.</b> The Canaanites were astonished that this particular cluster — that the children of Israel had cut it — was something novel and wondrous, for there were many clusters in the land as large as this one or larger, and it was not remarkable at all among the Canaanites, the inhabitants of the land. On account of this astonishment of theirs they called the place Nahal Eshkol."], :book :numbers, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:39:38.304036030Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}